    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Hainanese chicken rice is a dish of "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "poached",
            "zh": "水煮的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " chicken and "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "seasoned",
            "zh": "调好味的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " rice. It is seen as one of the national dishes of Singapore. The dish can also be found throughout Southeast Asia. In 2011, CNN listed chicken rice as one of the 50 best foods in the world."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "From the 1840s to the 1920s, early "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "immigrants",
            "ref": "v-immigrant"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " from Hainan came to Singapore. They brought with them a dish made from "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Wenchang chicken",
            "zh": "文昌鸡"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The chicken meat was served over rice and it was covered with thick oil. Later, "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Cantonese",
            "zh": "广东的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " cooking "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "influenced",
            "ref": "v-influence"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the development of chicken rice. Wenchang chicken was no longer used. Instead, white cut chicken, or bai qie ji, was used because it was softer."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Today, the first step in making Hainanese chicken rice is poaching the entire chicken. The real test for the dish is the rice. Each cook has his or her own "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "recipe",
            "ref": "v-recipe"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and secret "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "ingredients",
            "ref": "v-ingredient"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for making the best rice. The goal is for the rice to be tasty enough to be eaten "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "on its own",
            "ref": "v-on-ones-own"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ]
  },
